Week 1, Day 2 | 19 Oct 2026
Goal: Use IF logic to label and flag orders so problems stand out.

What I did

* Turned the sales data into an Excel Table and fixed its range so the totals and empty columns sat outside it
* Rebuilt Margin with IF so the 4 orders with no revenue show blank instead of #DIV/0!
* Built a Margin Flag column with a nested IF (Check, Low, OK)
* Built an Order Size column with IFS (Check, Large, Medium, Small)
* Used COUNTIF and SUMIF to count orders and total revenue for each band

Key results

* 11 orders have a margin under 20%, all Game Consoles at about 16%
* Large orders are 20% of orders but bring 66% of revenue
* Small orders are 54% of orders but only 10% of revenue

What I learned

* A blank ("") is text and Excel ranks text above numbers, so check for blanks first
* IFS stops at the first true test, so the order of the tests matters
* [@Col] means this row, Table1[Col] means the whole column and #Headers means the header cell only
* Use $ to lock a total cell before dragging a formula down
* A low-margin product like a console can still be worth selling if it drives high-margin add-ons

